  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an owner looking to preserve a hotel’s **individuality** in the Caribbean and Latin America, the strongest “soft” or *collection-style* affiliations to consider are **Marriott’s Autograph Collection and The Luxury Collection**, **Hilton’s Curio Collection and Tapestry Collection**, **IHG’s Vignette Collection**, **Wyndham’s Registry Collection Hotels**, and **Choice’s Ascend Hotel Collection**.[7][8][10][14]\n\nThese brands are specifically positioned to keep a property’s local character rather than converting it into a standardized chain hotel. Marriott has multiple CALA properties under **Autograph Collection** and **Luxury Collection**,[7][12] Hilton says **Curio Collection** expanded in Argentina, Brazil, and Colombia and **Tapestry Collection** debuted in Chile and Puerto Rico,[14] and IHG describes **Vignette Collection** as a curation of “distinct hand-picked hotels” offering one-of-a-kind stays.[6][10]\n\nIf you want the most regionally active options, the current footprint in the source set points to:\n\n- **Marriott Autograph Collection / Luxury Collection**: strong luxury presence across Caribbean and Latin America.[7][11][12]\n- **Hilton Curio Collection / Tapestry Collection**: explicitly growing in several CALA markets, with a boutique/independent feel.[14]\n- **IHG Vignette Collection / Kimpton / Hotel Indigo**: good fit for owners seeking lifestyle positioning and operational support while retaining identity.[6][10][16]\n- **Wyndham Registry Collection Hotels**: a soft-brand option mentioned in LATAM distribution.[4][16]\n- **Choice Ascend Hotel Collection**: widely represented across 20+ countries in Latin America and the Caribbean.[9]\n- **Radisson Individuals**: another collection-style option within Choice’s CALA portfolio.[9]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **shortlist by segment**—for example, *luxury resort*, *upper-upscale urban boutique*, or *all-inclusive independent resort*—and narrow the best brand match for a specific island or country.",
